8: # Quarkus TDD Workflow
9: 
10: TDD guidance for Quarkus 3.x services with 80%+ coverage (unit + integration). Optimized for event-driven architectures with Apache Camel.
11: 
12: ## When to Use
13: 
14: - New features or REST endpoints
15: - Bug fixes or refactors
16: - Adding data access logic, security rules, or reactive streams
17: - Testing Apache Camel routes and event handlers
18: - Testing event-driven services with RabbitMQ
19: - Testing conditional flow logic
20: - Validating CompletableFuture async operations
21: - Testing LogContext propagation
22: 
23: ## Workflow
24: 
25: 1. Write tests first (they should fail)
26: 2. Implement minimal code to pass
27: 3. Refactor with tests green
28: 4. Enforce coverage with JaCoCo (80%+ target)
29: 
30: ## Unit Tests with @Nested Organization
31: 
32: Follow this structured approach for comprehensive, readable tests:
33: 
34: ```java
35: @ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)
36: @DisplayName("OrderService Unit Tests")
37: class OrderServiceTest {
38: 
39:   @Mock
40:   private OrderRepository orderRepository;
41: 
42:   @Mock
43:   private EventService eventService;
44: 
45:   @Mock
46:   private FulfillmentPublisher fulfillmentPublisher;
47: 
48:   @InjectMocks
49:   private OrderService orderService;
50: 
51:   private CreateOrderCommand validCommand;
52: 
53:   @BeforeEach
54:   void setUp() {
55:     validCommand = new CreateOrderCommand(
56:         "customer-123",
57:         List.of(new OrderLine("sku-123", 2))
58:     );
59:   }
60: 
61:   @Nested
62:   @DisplayName("Tests for createOrder")
63:   class CreateOrder {
64: 
65:     @Test
66:     @DisplayName("Should persist order and publish fulfillment event")
67:     void givenValidCommand_whenCreateOrder_thenPersistsAndPublishes() {
68:       // ARRANGE
69:       doNothing().when(orderRepository).persist(any(Order.class));
70: 
71:       // ACT
72:       OrderReceipt receipt = orderService.createOrder(validCommand);
73: 
74:       // ASSERT
75:       assertThat(receipt).isNotNull();
76:       assertThat(receipt.customerId()).isEqualTo("customer-123");
77:       verify(orderRepository).persist(any(Order.class));
78:       verify(fulfillmentPublisher).publishAsync(receipt);
79:       verify(eventService).createSuccessEvent(receipt, "ORDER_CREATED");
80:     }
81: 
82:     @Test
83:     @DisplayName("Should reject missing customer id")
84:     void givenMissingCustomerId_whenCreateOrder_thenThrowsBadRequest() {
85:       // ARRANGE
86:       CreateOrderCommand invalid = new CreateOrderCommand("", validCommand.lines());
87: 
88:       // ACT & ASSERT
89:       WebApplicationException exception = assertThrows(
90:           WebApplicationException.class,
91:           () -> orderService.createOrder(invalid)
92:       );
93: 
94:       assertThat(exception.getResponse().getStatus()).isEqualTo(400);
95:       verify(orderRepository, never()).persist(any(Order.class));
96:       verify(fulfillmentPublisher, never()).publishAsync(any());
97:     }
98: 
99:     @Test
100:     @DisplayName("Should record error event when persistence fails")
101:     void givenPersistenceFailure_whenCreateOrder_thenRecordsErrorEvent() {
102:       // ARRANGE
103:       doThrow(new PersistenceException("database unavailable"))
104:           .when(orderRepository).persist(any(Order.class));
105: 
106:       // ACT & ASSERT
107:       PersistenceException exception = assertThrows(
108:           PersistenceException.class,
109:           () -> orderService.createOrder(validCommand)
110:       );
111: 
112:       assertThat(exception.getMessage()).contains("database unavailable");
113:       verify(eventService).createErrorEvent(
114:           eq(validCommand),
115:           eq("ORDER_CREATE_FAILED"),
116:           contains("database unavailable")
117:       );
118:       verify(fulfillmentPublisher, never()).publishAsync(any());
119:     }
120: 
121:     @Test
122:     @DisplayName("Should reject null commands")
123:     void givenNullCommand_whenCreateOrder_thenThrowsNullPointerException() {
124:       // ACT & ASSERT
125:       assertThrows(
126:           NullPointerException.class,
127:           () -> orderService.createOrder(null)
128:       );
129: 
130:       verify(orderRepository, never()).persist(any(Order.class));
131:     }
132:   }
133: }
134: ```
135: 
136: ### Key Testing Patterns
137: 
138: 1. **@Nested Classes**: Group tests by method being tested
139: 2. **@DisplayName**: Provide readable test descriptions for test reports
140: 3. **Naming Convention**: `givenX_whenY_thenZ` for clarity
141: 4. **AAA Pattern**: Explicit `// ARRANGE`, `// ACT`, `// ASSERT` comments
142: 5. **@BeforeEach**: Setup common test data to reduce duplication
143: 6. **assertDoesNotThrow**: Test success scenarios without catching exceptions
144: 7. **assertThrows**: Test exception scenarios with message validation using AssertJ
145: 8. **Comprehensive Coverage**: Test happy paths, null inputs, edge cases, exceptions
146: 9. **Verify Interactions**: Use Mockito `verify()` to ensure methods are called correctly
147: 10. **Never Verify**: Use `never()` to ensure methods are NOT called in error scenarios
